From 53a352f6c7d07d9b78e21c810b2ab3a49dd6e865 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Takumi Ando <takumi@spacecubics.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 14:40:54 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] spi: zynqmp_gqspi: Fix chip select for independent flashes

The GQSPI driver only selects CS1 when SPI NOR marks an operation as
accessing the upper device in a stacked-memory configuration. When that
flag is not set, the driver always selects CS0.

Independent flash devices do not use the stacked-memory flag, so a
device with reg = <1> is incorrectly accessed through CS0.

Use the physical chip select as the fallback when the stacked-memory
flag is not set. This preserves stacked-memory handling while allowing
independent devices on CS1 to be selected.

Signed-off-by: Takumi Ando <takumi@spacecubics.com>
---
 drivers/spi/zynqmp_gqspi.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/spi/zynqmp_gqspi.c b/drivers/spi/zynqmp_gqspi.c
index 4251bf28cd3..713bffda6df 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/zynqmp_gqspi.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/zynqmp_gqspi.c
@@ -860,7 +860,7 @@ static int zynqmp_qspi_exec_op(struct spi_slave *slave,
 	if (slave->flags & SPI_XFER_U_PAGE)
 		priv->u_page = 1;
 	else
-		priv->u_page = 0;
+		priv->u_page = spi_chip_select(slave->dev);
 
 	if ((slave->flags & GQSPI_SELECT_LOWER_CS) &&
 	    (slave->flags & GQSPI_SELECT_UPPER_CS))
-- 
2.55.0

